WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:02.752
(inspirational music)

00:00:02.752 --> 00:00:04.129
- Woo!

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:06.881
- Who am I rooting for this
year at the 95th Oscars?

00:00:06.881 --> 00:00:08.091
- It's an easy choice for me.

00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:10.135
"Everything Everywhere All at Once".

00:00:10.135 --> 00:00:12.762
- Like I said, "She's not most people."

00:00:12.762 --> 00:00:15.181
- This film was transcendent.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.767
- It takes the biggest swings,
takes the biggest risks.

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:18.601
(patrons screaming)

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:20.812
It's bonkers, but it
still has a heart to it.

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:24.274
- "The Fabelmans" is my favorite
95th Oscar nominated movie.

00:00:24.274 --> 00:00:26.776
- How'd you make it look like
The guns were really firing?

00:00:26.776 --> 00:00:29.988
- [Fan] It encapsulates
the movie magic we all feel

00:00:29.988 --> 00:00:31.573
when the lights begin to dim

00:00:31.573 --> 00:00:34.159
and we go somewhere we have been before.

00:00:34.159 --> 00:00:35.827
- The "Best Picture" nominated film

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:37.746
I'm rooting for is "Elvis",

00:00:37.746 --> 00:00:39.372
and I might be a little biased.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:43.376
I left the theater and I felt
like I was on another planet.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.838
- Now is the time.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.722
- I am rooting for "Avatar".

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:56.639
- You saved My Life.

00:00:56.639 --> 00:00:58.349
- [Fan] Just seeing it in the theaters

00:00:58.349 --> 00:01:00.226
took me to a different dimension.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.062
- The cinematography, the storyline,

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.354
the visuals were stunning.

00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:05.774
- The "Best Picture" film
that I am rooting for

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:08.359
is "The Banshees of Inisherin".

00:01:08.359 --> 00:01:10.820
- It's a film that I
really personally loved.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.656
- The scenery was hauntingly beautiful

00:01:13.656 --> 00:01:16.868
and Colin Farrell's
performance was brilliant.

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:17.911
- Stop running away from me

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.996
like some fool of a moody schoolchild.

00:01:19.996 --> 00:01:22.165
- "Top Gun: Maverick"
should win "Best Picture"

00:01:22.165 --> 00:01:26.294
because it really revitalized
the theater experience

00:01:26.294 --> 00:01:28.421
that brought everything to the table that

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.632
you would think that a "Top Gun" sequel

00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:32.008
would bring and then more.

00:01:32.008 --> 00:01:32.842
(plane explodes)

00:01:32.842 --> 00:01:35.220
- "Women Talking" should get
some Oscar love this year.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.429
- We may need to protect ourselves.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:39.182
- [Fan] I haven't got nervous
in a movie in a long time.

00:01:39.182 --> 00:01:40.850
- Here is why "Triangle of Sadness"

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.770
deserves to win "Best
Picture" at the Oscars.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:47.398
- It's always, "Yes sir, yes ma'am."

00:01:47.398 --> 00:01:49.901
- [Fan] Great plot, original
takes, awesome characters.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:51.319
- This year I'm rooting for

00:01:51.319 --> 00:01:53.029
"All Quiet on the Western Front".

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.368
- It's one of the most
terrorizing films I've ever seen,

00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:00.870
yet one of the most beautiful.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.248
(inspirational music continues)

